: Computers (2073-431X), 2025, v. 14, n. 3, p. 82, doi. 10.3390/computers14030082\n\nAuthors\n    \n\n## Nassreddine, Ghalia; Nassereddine, Mohamad; Al-Khatib, Obada\n\nAbstract\n    \n\n## Recent advancements across various sectors have resulted in a significant increase in the utilization of smart gadgets. This augmentation has resulted in an expansion of the network and the devices linked to it. Nevertheless, the development of the network has concurrently resulted in a rise in policy infractions impacting information security. Finding intruders immediately is a critical component of maintaining network security. The intrusion detection system is useful for network security because it can quickly identify threats and give alarms. In this paper, a new approach for network intrusion detection was proposed. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEnsemble Learning for Network Intrusion Detection Based on Correlation and Embedded Feature Selection Techniques (https://www.mdpi.com/2073-431X/14/3/82)\nciteturn12search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.6 years ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; Proposed approach for network intrusion detection based on ensemble learning technique ... Image: Computers 14 00082 g001 ... As shown in Figure 1, the proposed FS approach is composed of two techniques: correlation feature selection and the embedded algorithm. ... Enhancing intrusion detection in IoT networks using machine learning-based feature selection and ensemble models.\nImage: Computers 14 00082 g001\n\nFigure 1. FS approach based on CFS and embedded algorithm.\n\nAs shown in Figure 1, the proposed FS approach is composed of two techniques: correlation feature selection and the embedded algorithm.\n\n○\n    \n\nCorrelation-based feature selection (CFS): This is an approach for identifying feature subsets that reveal a high correlation with the target variable while providing a low correlation among the features in the identified subsets. The idea behind CFS is to select a subset of features that expand information concerning the target variable while minimizing redundancy included in the features. At the beginning, the CFS algorithm calculates the correlation between each feature and the target variable. After that, it assesses the correlation between each feature pair. Following this, it selects the subset of features exhibiting the strongest correlation with the target variable while maintaining the lowest correlation among themselves [27].\n\n○\n    \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEnsemble Learning for Network Intrusion Detection Based on Correlation... (https://bishtref.com/articles/10.3390/computers14030082)\nciteturn12search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.6 years ago; Crawled: last month;     82 ... G Ghalia Nassreddine Computer and Information Systems Department, Rafik Hariri University, Damour-Chouf 2010, Lebanon ... Ensemble Learning for Network Intrusion Detection Based on Correlation and Embedded Feature Selection Techniques.\n[50]\n\nSayem \"ENIDS: A Deep Learning-Based Ensemble Framework for Network Intrusion Detection Systems\" IEEE Trans. Netw. Serv. Manag. (2024) 10.1109/tnsm.2024.3414305\n\nShowing 50 of 52 references\n\nMetrics\n\n27\n\nCitations\n\n52\n\nReferences\n\nDetails\n\nPublished\n    Feb 25, 2025\n\nVol/Issue\n    14(3)\n\nPages\n    82\n\nLicense\n    View\n\nAuthors\n\nG Ghalia Nassreddine Computer and Information Systems Department, Rafik Hariri University, Damour-Chouf 2010, Lebanon\n\nM Mohamad Nassereddine School of Engineering, University of Wollongong in Dubai, Knowledge Village, Dubai P.O. Box 20183, United Arab Emirates\n\nO Obada Al-Khatib School of Engineering, University of Wollongong in Dubai, Knowledge Village, Dubai P.O. Box 20183, United Arab Emirates\n\nCite This Article\n\nGhalia Nassreddine, Mohamad Nassereddine, Obada Al-Khatib (2025). Ensemble Learning for Network Intrusion Detection Based on Correla